{"qid":"Q8733","names":["Qing Dynasty"],"title":"Qing Dynasty","endonym":{"native":"ᡩᠠᡳᠴᡳᠩ ᡤᡠᡵᡠᠨ","lang":"mnc"},"capsule":"The Qing dynasty, founded by the Manchu Aisin Gioro clan and established over China proper after the fall of Beijing in 1644, was the last imperial dynasty of China and the second largest contiguous empire in history at its height. Under the Qianlong Emperor (r. 1735–1796) it absorbed Xinjiang, Tibet, and Mongolia, reaching an area of approximately 13 million square kilometers. The 19th century brought a sequence of crises: the Opium Wars (1839–1842, 1856–1860) forced unequal treaties and treaty-port concessions; the Taiping Rebellion (1850–1864) killed perhaps 20–30 million people; and defeat in the First Sino-Japanese War (1894–1895) cost Taiwan. The dynasty collapsed after the Xinhai Revolution, with the last emperor Puyi abdicating in February 1912.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Inner territories are well documented from imperial gazeteers, military maps, and the Qing's own cartographic surveys (the Kangxi Atlas of 1718); frontier zones in Siberia, Central Asia, and the Mongolian steppe carry moderate uncertainty; overall confidence is high for the heartland, moderate for outer tributaries.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Qing dynasty","url":"https://www.britannica.com/topic/Qing-dynasty"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Qing dynasty","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qing_dynasty"}],"britannica":"topic/Qing-dynasty","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Qing dynasty","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Nurhaci (Tianming Emperor)","nativeName":"努爾哈赤","roman":"Nǔ'ěrhāchì","start":1616